From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 18:10:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: gemini-station: weight the LL cluster's
 power share

The power allocator splits its budget in proportion to each actor's
weighted power request. A cluster's request is its energy-model power at
its current point, so the cheaper LL cluster asks for less, gets less,
and steps down further. Under 8-CPU load at the 75 C target it fell to
221 MHz while the L cluster kept most of the budget.

Both clusters are Cortex-A53, so a MHz is worth the same on either. For
a budget near 1 W, LL at its top point with L around 650 MHz is within
1 % of the best split, and LL at 221 MHz is about 22 % below it.

Give the LL control map a contribution of 4096 and the L and GPU maps
1024. With these weights, set at run time on the station, LL stayed at
1547 MHz in 53 of 60 samples and the work done under the 75 C target
rose 10.8 % over equal weights, with the junction at 73.5-76.9 C.
---
 .../boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station-dvfs.dts | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station-dvfs.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station-dvfs.dts
index 4feb0d924..5904e09c4 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station-dvfs.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station-dvfs.dts
@@ -364,6 +364,12 @@ vproc2: BUCKB {
  * from the station tree stay for the step-wise governor. The zone's policy
  * is set to power_allocator at run time. sustainable-power is a first
  * estimate, below the 1.9 W at which 8-CPU load still warmed past 70 C.
+ *
+ * The allocator splits the budget in proportion to each actor's weighted
+ * request. With equal weights the LL cluster, which asks for less power per
+ * MHz, is pushed to its lowest point while the L cluster keeps most of the
+ * budget. Weighting LL four times lets it keep its top point, which is
+ * within 1 % of the best split of a ~1 W budget between the two A53 clusters.
  */
 &{/thermal-zones/soc-thermal} {
 	polling-delay-passive = <100>;
@@ -380,6 +386,7 @@ soc_control: soc-control {
 	cooling-maps {
 		map-control-ll {
 			trip = <&soc_control>;
+			contribution = <4096>;
 			cooling-device =
 				<&cpu0 THERMAL_NO_LIMIT THERMAL_NO_LIMIT>,
 				<&cpu1 THERMAL_NO_LIMIT THERMAL_NO_LIMIT>,
@@ -389,6 +396,7 @@ map-control-ll {
 
 		map-control-l {
 			trip = <&soc_control>;
+			contribution = <1024>;
 			cooling-device =
 				<&cpu4 THERMAL_NO_LIMIT THERMAL_NO_LIMIT>,
 				<&cpu5 THERMAL_NO_LIMIT THERMAL_NO_LIMIT>,
@@ -398,6 +406,7 @@ map-control-l {
 
 		map-control-gpu {
 			trip = <&soc_control>;
+			contribution = <1024>;
 			cooling-device = <&gpu THERMAL_NO_LIMIT THERMAL_NO_LIMIT>;
 		};
 	};
